ng supply  points to buy from supply lines the  supply line is like a miniature battle  pass where you have to go from one rank  to the next using supply points to  unlock the items  thankfully the supply points aren't hard  to come by as you unlock them after  completing a level but as we'll see it's  not that easy  the deck builder is really nice too as  you have a set amount of cards you can  put into a deck and then you can take  them into the campaign  these are very helpful as you select one  each level and find a card box to get a  random card in the middle of the level  these are necessary to surviving as the  point of the game is to get stronger as  you progress since the difficulty at  least past the beginning one is very  unforgiving  outside the fort is a shooting range and  one of the best parts of the game it has  every weapon from primaries to  secondaries to melee as well as every  attachment in the game so not only can  you figure out what weapons suit your  playstyle but also what attachments go  good with those guns  after you're satisfied you can then  search or create a game once you've  spawned in you can go through a couple  menus like picking your cleaner as well  as a variety of cards you want to start  with the cleaner you pick will stay with  you for the entire run so you have to  choose wisely as each one of them is  actually different than the other not  only do they each have a different  starter weapon they have different buffs  and equipment evangelo for example has  the ability to break out of guards once  every 60 seconds so the team doesn't  need to help him in sticky situations  but mom can revive anyone within a  couple seconds once per level which is  extremely helpful they also provide  small team wide buffs like more stamina  more health or more movement speed  these aren't going to completely shift  the gameplay as that's where the cards  come in but they're just small  nice passive buffs to make the character  just that little more powerful after the  game starts but before you leave the  area you can buy  items from the shop with copper which  can be found or earned throughout the  levels  copper can be used to refill health and  ammo as well as buy guns attachments and  more equipment ammo guns and equipment  do exist out in the world so it's not  necessary to buy them from here but  sometimes the items are better than the  world drops  on the beginning difficulty you'll find  yourself with more copper than you can  spend  the game does tweak this problem albeit  slightly eventually the rarity of  equipment like bandages and first aid  kits become uncommon rarity which means  they'll heal you for more but they also  cost a little bit more  too in the time that i played the  medical equipment went as high as  uncommon but i'm assuming in the higher  difficulties and maybe even in the  future acts when the main game releases  this will change for the time i was able  to play  i was having fun this game is really fun  with friends i'm not entirely sure how  it feels solo but i can't imagine being  too fun especially when the difficulty  gets really high and you have to rely on  bots to save you  i tried to play solo but the solo  campaign option isn't available right  now and when you set your game to  private it just won't let you start a  game  the only way to get a solo game in the  beta is to queue for a match and hope  the players leave really early on in the  level  also another side note as i noticed this  while editing it seems the game is also  entirely online so you cannot play a  solo campaign  offline which is quite said here earlier  i mentioned i enjoy the game  when i'm able to play it and that the  campaign was finished around 2 hours and  i played versus for an hour  yet i also said that i played for 6  hours in total  so what was i doing during those extra  three hours  crashing out of the eight levels i only  finished one of them from start to  finish  every other level i crashed at least  once in sometimes i was back in my  friend's lobby within 30 seconds  sometimes i'd be going 10 plus minutes  since apparently the server was  unavailable or full which was completely  false  this turned me off the game so much i  wasn't playing the campaign and merely  just being dragged along while my  friends actually played the game  apparently though just as the characters  in this game are diverse apparently our  crashes were diverse as well  i couldn't stay in a campaign game for  more than five minutes most times but  while my friend was completely fine in  campaign he'd have an issue  queueing for a versus game and couldn't  stay in our lobby for more than five  minutes it took us 25 minutes to find a  match at one point and the one time we  found one i got disconnected immediately  so i pretty much wasted 30 minutes for  nothing  speaking of those versus matches i've  only been able to get into  three lobbies in the over one hour of  queue time and not once did it go past  round two  each game i played i either disconnected  or the enemy team left meaning we would  win by forfeit  since neither team reached three points  because of the four foot win i've  actually never fully completed a game of  verses yet this is incredibly pathetic  you wait around 10 minutes for the match  to start then you wait 2 minutes for the  survivors to pick their characters and  loadout another minute for them to  scavenge around all the gear to prepare  for the fight  only for the round to end in 3 minutes  then you do it again but switch teams  you now have to go through three minutes  of waiting for menus and picking your  loadout in character and scavenging only  to die in about two to three minutes  it's like eighty percent waiting and  twenty percent gameplay which is  ultimately just not fun speaking of  gameplay  let's talk about that firstly if you  play on console  enjoy never needing to aim again if you  played the first mission of modern  warfare 2  you'll know what i mean and you've  probably even noticed it in the gameplay  already but the first clip i'm about to  show  is either me spamming or holding the  shoot button while just aiming this of  course thanks to recoil would cause my  gun to go up and past the target  the other is me spamming the left  trigger so that i'm constantly aiming  then not aiming then back to aiming  again  as like most games aim assist can help  with snapping to targets although it's  very  minor this game is very different  however  pay attention to the ping noise as the  more pings you hear the more time i hit  the target  do you see how broken that is it looked  like i had zero recoil and i'm such a  pro  at aiming that i can control the spray  pattern of my gun but that couldn't be  farther from the truth  it looks a lot worse in game two i  literally cannot tell you what i'm  shooting at in this clip  all i know is i'm killing something and  that's about it and that's also only at  50 strength according to the setting  if you want to play with normal aim  assist i'd recommend about  20 to 30 but why would you when it's  this laughably broken another setting  that needs talking about is fov  simply put there is no console fov  slider it's not the end of the world but  the camera is just a little too close  for my comfort and it's more of a  personal preference as i know not  everybody cares about the setting but i  thought it was worth talking about since  we are on the topic of personal  preference let me go over some things  that i  dislike a bit while the gunplay is  pretty good minus the aim assist of  course  some guns don't feel like there's any  weight behind them the de-gol the magnum  and the super 90 just don't feel  powerful at all  this is quite ironic since the other  weapons even the ones in the same class  sound wonderful  the other dislike i have is actually  both the characters and the special  infected now maybe it's just because we  haven't had enough time to get to know  them yet but i don't feel connected to  these characters at all  even a decade later i could still name  you the four characters of left 4 dead 2  but  talk to me a month after release i might  not even remember half these characters  names there just seems to be no  personality behind them there is one  thing i like however and that's the  small bit of lore that gets dropped  during the discussions like finding out  that mom's son was killed and that she's  still mourning his loss  sadly this doesn't happen often and when  it does it's kind of hard to pay  attention to this stuff when you're  getting swarmed by hordes of infected  but  more of this would be really perfect the  special infected bother me for a couple  reasons as well  firstly is that there's no way to tell  when they arrive other than the  subtitles  without the subtitles i wouldn't have  figured out a special infected was on  the map left 2 had some sound cues that  played when a specific special infected  was nearby which was both smart and  helpful this does not exist in back for  blood however  the issues that bother me with most of  these is that the families the game has  the infected are split into families  tall boys reekers and stingers  all tall boys are the big guys with one  large arm the reekers all blow up and  cause a lot of chaos while the stingers  attack from long range  this is really cool but especially when  i'm really focusing in the game i can't  tell the difference between them one of  the tall boys called the crusher grabs  the enemy and crushes them while the  bruiser slams his fist on the ground  causing aoe damage  the only difference i see in them is  that one has small spikes on his arm and  the other doesn't  that doesn't help me in the slightest  knowing who i'm facing is crucial to  surviving  and i'd argue it's even worse with the  reekers as one vomits acid while the  other just explodes if i know which one  it is i can prioritize them if it's the  reeker that vomits i should shoot him  first since he has long range but if i  see the suicide reeker and he's far away  i have a bit more time before i need to  act there are differences yes but not  any that you would notice before it's  too late too many times i was calling  out the special infected on the map only  to get it wrong since they look the same  literally just making one of them each  type and not having any families would  have been great  yes the crusher is kind of like the  charger the reekers or boomers and the  stingers or the spitter from left for  dead too but  who cares at this point it's practically  a left 4 dead game and i'm ok with those  infected types  so long as i know who i'm facing that's  what i liked about left 4 dead there was  only one spitter or only 1 hunter there  wasn't one spitter that spits acid the  other one spits oil it was just one  it may sound boring only having one  specific special infected per type like  that but i believe it's more beneficial  to having an overall enjoyable game  regardless with all these issues there  were  quite a few times i was enjoying myself  and what helped this a lot was these  encounters and corruption cards and i  want to use this time to offer another  suggestion  in mission 1-2 after walking only a  couple yards from the safe house this  thing called an ogre spawns after some  time it disappears but then reappears  again at the end of the level this  adds a new bit of difficulty to the game  which was great in 2-2 there's an  excellent corruption card added to this  level corruption cards are essentially  cards that change the game a bit by  giving you challenges to earn more  copper or just outright changing  something in the map like stronger  enemies this one added fog to the game  which made it harder to see which led to  us getting ambushed quite a bit  this was genius but it's not at its  highest potential take this  and randomize it i don't want the ogre  to spawn only on 1-2 or the fog on 2-2  make the fog spawn during the finale i  want these to be random as i'm going to  create  characters and builds around this  situation and i don't want that  having this would easily surpass left 4  dead in replayability as there was no  change in the gameplay from level to  level only a difficulty meter they have  an excellent tool at their disposal i  just  really hope they utilize it what could  help this mechanic skyrocket its  potential is campaign verses  but sadly that does not exist i know  there's been a lot of debate  about this some saying only the elitist  of left 4 dead care about this game mode  while the others say it should be  required for a game like this  personally i agree with the latter the  versus mode we have now  is fun assuming the players actually  stay in the game but i can see it  getting boring really  quickly the fun of the campaign versus  mode has always been about utilizing  your knowledge of the infected and the  map to create problems for the survivors  and it could work just as well in back  for blood and since there's probably  going to be more levels than left 4 dead  this seems like even more of a reason to  do so the survivors get stronger with  cards while the infected gets stronger  with the upgrade system  both teams have the knowledge of the map  and what to do and with the addition of  these corruption cards and encounters i  mentioned earlier this ultimately  creates an intense experience and i feel  like it would be a waste if this  wasn't added so for my final thoughts of  the game  honestly i would wait to see where this  goes i still stand by my original  statement that back for blood has  potential but it needs to sort out some  issues first and the 60  plus season pass price tag really isn't  helping it has a somewhat lackluster pvp  experience and  so far a decent campaign but both have  been corrupted with awful connection  issues  completely turning me off from giving  the game another try regardless  thank you for making it this far in the  video if you've played back for blood  yourself let me know what you thought  about it in the comments down below  with that thank you for watching the  video today if you're new make sure to  subscribe for more reviews like this and  check out some of my other reviews and  essays as well  if you're a returning viewer i thank you  for coming back and as always  take care everyone goodbye  [Music]  you

